  {
    "id": "books",
    "shortLabel": "Books",
    "title": "Books & Literature",
    "text": "Books across physics, computational mechanics, mathematics, and hard science fiction that fundamentally reshaped how I think.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "title": "The Feynman Lectures on Physics",
        "subtitle": "Richard P. Feynman",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532012164546-f432f2e3777f?w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
        "thought": "Feynman's intuition for classical mechanics and electromagnetism taught me to visualize physical principles before touching a differential equation. It is the purest benchmark for conceptual clarity in engineering.",
        "link": "https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Finite Element Procedures",
        "subtitle": "Klaus-Jürgen Bathe",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544716278-ca5e3f4abd8c?w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
        "thought": "The definitive foundation for nonlinear solid mechanics and continuum element formulations. Walking through continuum kinematics and arc-length solver algorithms gave me the exact rigor to write numerical solvers.",
        "link": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Golden Braid",
        "subtitle": "Douglas Hofstadter",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512820790803-83ca734da794?w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
        "thought": "A masterpiece connecting formal logic, recursive self-reference, Bach's canons, and cognitive emergence. It bridged formal mathematics with aesthetics in a way that stayed with me forever.",
        "link": ""
      },
      {
        "title": "The Three-Body Problem Trilogy",
        "subtitle": "Liu Cixin",
        "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1462331940025-496dfbfc7564?w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
        "thought": "The cosmic sociology and dimensional collapse concepts made this the most mind-bending hard science fiction I have ever read. The Dark Forest axiom gave me a genuine sense of cosmic awe and dread.",
        "link": ""
      }
    ]
  },
